Parallel factorization Options exposes parallel (Parallel::Off, On, or Choose),parallel_type (ParallelType::Tree, Node, or Both), and threads.The defaults are Choose, Both, and zero (available CPU parallelism).Set threads: 1 to run serially. Off creates no worker pool and retainsserial ordering selection and the up-looking augmented-system fast path. use baldes::extensions::ipm::{Options, Parallel, ParallelType};
